    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0019" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/1388</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-01">November 1, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Lord Halifax called this morning and said he was very happy to have me
                        here.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d6-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>He left an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d6-f2"
                    /> with me relative to the possibility of sending two people to London to
                    discuss Middle Eastern affairs with the Foreign Office. I am sending copies to
                    Messrs. Murray<anchor n="4" xml:id="d6-f3"/> and Matthews.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d6-f4"/> He suggested that if it were possible for Mr. Wallace
                    Murray to go there quickly and to keep Colonel Hoskins<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d6-f5"/> there to attend the conference, it would be very helpful to
                    the Foreign Office.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="2" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Stettinius had entered the Department as Under Secretary of State on October
                    4, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f2" n="3" xml:id="d6-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f3" n="4" xml:id="d6-f3-content">
                <p>Wallace Murray, Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f4" n="5" xml:id="d6-f4-content">
                <p>H. Freeman Matthews, Chief of the Division of European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f5" n="6" xml:id="d6-f5-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Harold B. Hoskins, Personal Representative of President Roosevelt in the
                    Near East in 1942–13, at this time on a mission to London regarding Palestine
                    problems; see <ref target="#pg747">pp. 747</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
